This C# implementation provides a modular, production-ready, and thread-safe **Enterprise E-Commerce Checkout Orchestrator** without external dependencies. 

It is divided into three distinct modules:
1. **Shopping Cart Validation Engine**: Formulates parallelized validation checks (stock, stale pricing, and order limits) utilizing a composite rule-based approach.
2. **Saga Transaction Coordinator**: Coordinates cross-microservice operations (Inventory, Payment, Shipping) with complete automated rollback capabilities under failure conditions.
3. **Invoice Generator**: Formats and generates standard-compliant, binary-safe PDF documents containing billing statements, line-item tables, and tax details using raw byte streams.

---

### Core Domain Models

Save the following domain definitions as the baseline architecture for the entire system:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace EnterpriseCheckout.Domain
{
    public record CartItem(string ProductId, string SKU, string Name, decimal UnitPrice, int Quantity);

    public record Cart(string CartId, string CustomerId, List<CartItem> Items, string PromoCode = null);

    public record ProductCatalogItem(string ProductId, string SKU, string Name, decimal CurrentPrice, int AvailableStock);

    public record ValidationFailure(string PropertyName, string ErrorMessage);

    public record ValidationResult(bool IsSuccess, List<ValidationFailure> Errors, decimal SubTotal, decimal Discount, decimal Tax, decimal TotalPrice);

    public record SagaState
    {
        public string TransactionId { get; init; } = Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
        public string CartId { get; init; }
        public string CustomerId { get; init; }
        public List<CartItem> Items { get; init; } = new();
        public decimal TotalAmount { get; init; }

        // Step States for Rollback Tracker
        public string InventoryReservationId { get; set; }
        public bool IsInventoryReserved { get; set; }
        public string PaymentTransactionId { get; set; }
        public bool IsPaymentCaptured { get; set; }
        public string ShippingTrackingId { get; set; }
        public bool IsShippingBooked { get; set; }
        public decimal ShippingCost { get; set; }
    }

    public record OrderDetails(
        string OrderId,
        string CustomerId,
        List<CartItem> Items,
        decimal SubTotal,
        decimal Discount,
        decimal Tax,
        decimal ShippingCost,
        decimal TotalAmount,
        string TransactionId,
        string TrackingId,
        DateTime OrderDate
    );
}
```

